1
00:00:23,790 --> 00:00:25,020
Hi, Grandpa.

2
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:26,710
Hi, Robbie.

3
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:28,050
Can I help?

4
00:00:28,050 --> 00:00:30,140
Yes, indeed.

5
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:33,410
Hand me two eggs from the refrigerator,

6
00:00:33,410 --> 00:00:37,800
and I'll make you two fried eggs.

7
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:40,030
How about some bacon?

8
00:00:40,030 --> 00:00:43,020
I made enough for an army.

9
00:00:43,020 --> 00:00:45,470
You going to the baseball game today?

10
00:00:45,470 --> 00:00:49,880
It's a perfect day for it--a little cloudy but nice and warm.

11
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:52,030
Dad and I were planning to go to the game,

12
00:00:52,030 --> 00:00:53,610
but he has to work today,

13
00:00:53,610 --> 00:00:55,470
and my friends don't want to go.

14
00:00:55,470 --> 00:00:57,910
It's not an important game, anyway.

15
00:00:57,910 --> 00:01:00,520
Do you have any other plans for the day?

16
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:02,510
I'll work on my computer.

17
00:01:02,510 --> 00:01:05,810
I have a new math program, and I want to learn how to use it.

18
00:01:05,810 --> 00:01:07,300
Maybe you can teach me

19
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:09,050
how to work on a computer someday.

20
00:01:09,050 --> 00:01:12,800
Anytime. It's really easy, but, like anything,

21
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:17,160
you need to work at it, Grandpa.

22
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:18,700
This bacon is great.

23
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:21,380
I love crispy bacon.

24
00:01:21,380 --> 00:01:23,830
Oh, what are you doing tomorrow?

25
00:01:23,830 --> 00:01:26,510
Nothing much.

26
00:01:26,510 --> 00:01:31,580
Well, maybe your dad and I could take you fishing with us.

27
00:01:31,580 --> 00:01:33,300
I'd like that, but ...

28
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:35,830
But what?

29
00:01:35,830 --> 00:01:37,960
But Dad is always so busy.

30
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:43,470
Well, can you come fishing with me tomorrow?

31
00:01:43,470 --> 00:01:47,530
Sure, I can.

32
00:01:47,530 --> 00:01:50,420
Robbie says you can't take him to the game today.

33
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:51,920
I really feel bad about it,

34
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:53,720
but they need me at the hospital today,

35
00:01:53,720 --> 00:01:55,320
in the children's ward.

36
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:57,780
I understand.

37
00:01:57,780 --> 00:02:00,190
Maybe we can spend some time together next weekend.

38
00:02:00,190 --> 00:02:01,470
Definitely.

39
00:02:01,470 --> 00:02:02,560
We should.

40
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:05,810
You and Robbie and me.

41
00:02:05,810 --> 00:02:08,240
Remember our first fishing trip?

42
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:10,160
I sure do....

43
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:13,860
Well, I've got to run, Dad.

44
00:02:13,860 --> 00:02:17,130
See you later.

45
00:02:17,130 --> 00:02:18,570
Going fishing?

46
00:02:18,570 --> 00:02:22,260
I'm thinking about it....

47
00:02:22,260 --> 00:02:23,750
So, how's work?

48
00:02:23,750 --> 00:02:26,880
Oh, the usual problems.

49
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:29,170
You're working pretty hard these days.

50
00:02:29,170 --> 00:02:33,590
I guess I am.

51
00:02:33,590 --> 00:02:37,380
When did you last go fishing with Robbie?

52
00:02:37,380 --> 00:02:39,710
I remember exactly.

53
00:02:39,710 --> 00:02:44,550
It was on his birthday, June second, two years ago.

54
00:02:44,550 --> 00:02:48,240
We didn't catch anything.

55
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:50,030
Remember our fishing trips?

56
00:02:50,030 --> 00:02:55,560
Yes. I loved them.

57
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:59,530
Remember catching your first fish?

58
00:02:59,530 --> 00:03:00,430
How can I forget?

59
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:05,210
I fell out of the boat!

60
00:03:05,210 --> 00:03:07,450
We had some good times together.

61
00:03:07,450 --> 00:03:10,360
Yes, we did.

62
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:13,930
Maybe we should do it again.

63
00:03:13,930 --> 00:03:16,010
How about tomorrow?

64
00:03:16,010 --> 00:03:17,520
Don't you have to work?

65
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:20,310
My paper work will wait.

66
00:03:20,310 --> 00:03:23,110
Oh, Robbie will be thrilled.

67
00:03:23,110 --> 00:03:25,100
I am, too, Son.

68
00:03:25,100 --> 00:03:27,000
I want to spend more time with Robbie.

69
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,940
Tomorrow.

70
00:03:28,940 --> 00:03:31,330
It'll be like old times for you and me.

71
00:03:31,330 --> 00:03:34,520
And Robbie will love it.

72
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:38,040
Well, what's the weather going to be like?

73
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:45,140
Radio says sunny and mild.

74
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:49,390
Well, I'll tell Robbie.

75
00:03:49,390 --> 00:03:53,230
And thanks, Dad.

76
00:03:53,230 --> 00:03:54,440
Don't thank me.

77
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:57,440
I'm just being a grandfather.
